---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: record detail" description="The screen behind every list row: what this record is, what state it is in, and what has happened to it.">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Who uses it</strong>: whoever owns this record, checking its
    status or adding to its history — a buyer, an approver, anyone who
    clicked in from a list row. <strong>How often</strong>: every time a
    list row is opened — this is the default landing for "tell me about
    this one," many times a day across a team. <strong>What "done" looks
    like</strong>: the
    current state is read in one glance, without opening anything else. The
    composed detail screen behind any list row: record cards, a status
    timeline, and an audit trail stacked in a feed — all standard components,
    generic to any ERP. This example is a purchase order; the shape is the
    same for an invoice, a change request, or a leave request.
    <strong>Not once the record stops fitting in one scan</strong> — when a
    reader has to hunt for a section, it wants anchor navigation and a
    sticky action bar, which is
    <a href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>object page</a>. Same content,
    different reading problem.
  </p>

  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol class="bo-breadcrumb">
      <li><a href={base + '/patterns/list-report'}>Cost centers</a></li>
      <li><a href="#">CC-4021</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">PO-88213</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The screen</h2>
    {/* IDENTITY LINE — what the document is, and what state it is in, on one
        line with the actions. MEASURED: 36px at 1440 (one row) and 68px at
        390, where the actions wrap to a second row — both inside the 80px
        budget (roadmap 24.6).
        Composed entirely from shipped primitives — a split cluster, the type
        badge and a status badge — so it is a documented shape, not a new
        component. Status lives HERE and is deliberately not repeated in the
        facts strip below. */}
    <div class="bo-cluster bo-cluster--split" style="margin-block-end: var(--bo-space-3)">
      <span class="bo-cluster">
        <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">Purchase order</span>
        <strong class="bo-u-tabular">PO-88213</strong>
        <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--success">Approved</span>
      </span>
      <span class="bo-cluster">
        <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="button">Print</button>
        <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="button">Copy</button>
      </span>
    </div>
    <article class="bo-widget" style="margin-block-end: var(--bo-space-4)">
      <div class="bo-widget__body">
        <dl class="bo-kv">
          <div><dt>Vendor</dt><dd>Umbrella Logistics</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Cost center</dt><dd>CC-4021</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Payment terms</dt><dd>Net 30</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Total</dt><dd class="bo-u-tabular">$12,400.00</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Requested</dt><dd><time datetime="2026-08-10">10 Aug 2026</time></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </article>
    <div class="bo-grid" style="--bo-grid-min: 20rem">
      <!-- Left: the record feed -->
      <div class="bo-stack">
        <article class="bo-widget">
          <header class="bo-widget__header">
            <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">Purchase Order #88213</span>
            <span class="bo-byline"><strong>R. Vance</strong> · Requester</span>
            <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--success">Approved</span>
          </header>
          <div class="bo-widget__body">
            <ol class="bo-ordered-list"><li>SKU-3391 · Standing desk (×4)</li><li>SKU-1180 · Monitor arm (×8)</li></ol>
          </div>
          <footer class="bo-widget__band bo-widget__band--msg">Approved by J. Kim · 12 Aug 2026, 10:15</footer>
        </article>

        <article class="bo-widget">
          <header class="bo-widget__header">
            <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">Goods Receipt #GR-88</span>
            <span class="bo-byline"><strong>M. Okafor</strong> · Warehouse</span>
            <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning">Partial</span>
          </header>
          <div class="bo-widget__body">
            <ol class="bo-ordered-list"><li>SKU-3391 · 4 of 4 received</li><li>SKU-1180 · 5 of 8 received</li></ol>
          </div>
          <footer class="bo-widget__band bo-widget__band--msg">Awaiting the remaining 3 monitor arms.</footer>
        </article>

        <!-- Trailing composer: the empty card IS the create form -->
        <article class="bo-widget">
          <header class="bo-widget__header"><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">Add record</span></header>
          <div class="bo-widget__body bo-cluster">
            <input class="bo-input" aria-label="Add a record to this order" placeholder="New goods receipt, invoice, or note…" />
            <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary">Add</button>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: status + audit -->
      <div class="bo-stack">
        <div>
          <h2 style="font-size: var(--bo-font-size-sm); color: var(--bo-color-text-muted)">Status</h2>
          <ol class="bo-timeline" role="list">
            <li class="bo-timeline__step" data-state="done"><span class="bo-timeline__marker" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><div class="bo-timeline__title"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Completed: </span>Requested</div><div class="bo-timeline__meta">R. Vance · 10 Aug</div></div></li>
            <li class="bo-timeline__step" data-state="done"><span class="bo-timeline__marker" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><div class="bo-timeline__title"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Completed: </span>Approved</div><div class="bo-timeline__meta">J. Kim · 12 Aug</div></div></li>
            <li class="bo-timeline__step" data-state="current" aria-current="step"><span class="bo-timeline__marker" aria-hidden="true">●</span><div><div class="bo-timeline__title">Receiving</div><div class="bo-timeline__meta">partial · 5 of 8</div></div></li>
            <li class="bo-timeline__step" data-state="pending"><span class="bo-timeline__marker" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div><div class="bo-timeline__title"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Not started: </span>Invoiced</div></div></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 style="font-size: var(--bo-font-size-sm); color: var(--bo-color-text-muted)">Audit trail</h2>
          <ol class="bo-audit" role="list">
            <li class="bo-audit__entry"><time class="bo-audit__time" datetime="2026-08-10T09:08">08-10 09:08</time><span><span class="bo-audit__actor">R. Vance</span> raised PO-88213</span></li>
            <li class="bo-audit__entry"><time class="bo-audit__time" datetime="2026-08-12T10:15">08-12 10:15</time><span><span class="bo-audit__actor">J. Kim</span> approved</span><span class="bo-audit__detail">"Within CC-4021 budget."</span></li>
            <li class="bo-audit__entry">
              <time class="bo-audit__time" datetime="2026-08-13T14:02">08-13 14:02</time>
              <span><span class="bo-audit__actor">M. Okafor</span> changed 2 fields on receipt</span>
              <span class="bo-audit__detail">
                {/* A field-level diff: .bo-data-table + badge, zero new CSS.
                    Two-channel by construction — the badge TEXT carries Added/
                    Removed/Modified, same rule as Amount's --negative and the
                    calendar's data-day="closed" (roadmap 53.3: scored, not
                    built as a component — see the grill for why). */}
                <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
                  <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
                    <caption class="bo-visually-hidden">Fields changed on this receipt</caption>
                    <thead>
                      <tr><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">Old</th><th scope="col">New</th><th scope="col">Change</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                      <tr>
                        <td>Qty received</td>
                        <td><span class="bo-u-tabular">3</span></td>
                        <td><span class="bo-u-tabular">5</span></td>
                        <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning">Modified</span></td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td>Status</td>
                        <td>Partial</td>
                        <td>Partial</td>
                        <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning">Modified</span></td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
              </span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The document frame — measured, not asserted</h2>
    <p>An ERP document screen is read far more often than it is edited, so the
    chrome above the content is a recurring tax. The shape here is
    <strong>one identity line</strong> — what the document is, which one, what
    state it is in, and the actions — then the facts, then the content:</p>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">Region</th>
          <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">1440px</th>
          <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">390px</th>
          <th scope="col">Note</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Identity line</td><td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">36px</td><td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">68px</td><td>one row on desktop; actions wrap to a second row on a phone</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Facts strip</td><td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">124px</td><td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">277px</td><td>five facts, auto-fit — this is content, not chrome, and it scrolls</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Facts strip <em>before</em></td><td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">127px</td><td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">331px</td><td>six facts: Status was repeated here and in the line above</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted" style="margin-block-start: var(--bo-space-3)">
    <strong>Zero new components.</strong> The identity line is a split
    <a href={base + '/base/primitives'}>cluster</a> holding the
    <a href={base + '/components/badge'}>type badge</a>, the record number and
    a status badge — all shipped. A dedicated document-header component would
    be a second way to do what a cluster already does.</p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Two rules worth keeping: <strong>status lives in
    the identity line, not in the facts</strong> — it was in both, which cost
    54px at phone width for a fact the reader had already seen; and
    <strong>put the actions in the line, not in a bar of their own</strong>,
    because a separate action bar is another band of chrome competing for the
    same vertical space. The
    <a href={base + '/patterns/detail-form'}>detail form</a> uses the same
    line; before this it had no identity region at all, so nothing on screen
    said which purchase order you were editing.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Breadcrumb</strong> — <a href={base + '/components/breadcrumb'}>breadcrumb</a>; where this record sits, and how users get back to the filtered list.</li>
      <li><strong>Facts strip</strong> — <a href={base + '/components/kv'}>key-value facts</a> (<code>.bo-kv</code>) for the header facts (vendor, cost centre, total): display data, never readonly inputs.</li>
      <li><strong>Record feed</strong> — one <a href={base + '/components/dashboard#card'}>card</a> per related document (order, receipt, invoice) in chronological order.</li>
      <li><strong>Status timeline + audit trail</strong> — <a href={base + '/components/approval-workflow'}>timeline and audit trail</a>: where it is now, and every state change with actor and timestamp.
      This is the human-monitoring signal: the actor column is where an
      agent's own changes become visible to the human owning the record.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Follows the <a href={base + '/concepts/review-anatomy'}>review-screen anatomy</a>
    contract — this is the short-record shape; see that page for when to reach
    for <a href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>object page</a> or
    <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval</a> instead.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /po/:id</td><td>the full screen. 404 → the not-found screen, same as any deep link to a record that no longer exists</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /po/:id/records</td><td>one new card fragment appended to the feed</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /po/:id/audit?after=…</td><td>newer audit entries for polling; empty body when nothing changed. 5xx/timeout: the per-section alert in States, not a page-level failure — the facts strip and feed already rendered and must stay readable</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><strong>The AI-manages / human-monitors
    split, stated</strong>: any actor — human or agent — can append to the
    feed or the audit trail through the same endpoints; the human's
    channel is the audit trail's actor column, where an automated change
    is as visible as a person's.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Loading</td><td>skeleton cards in the feed; the facts strip renders from the record itself, so it never blanks</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Empty feed</td><td>the record exists with no related documents yet — say so and offer the first action</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Error loading a section</td><td>a per-section alert; one failed audit fetch must not blank the record</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Read-only</td><td>no composer, no action buttons — the timeline and facts are the whole screen</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stale (someone else acted)</td><td>poll or push the timeline fragment; a decided record showing "awaiting approval" is the failure mode to avoid</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No JS</td><td>fully functional — this page has no JS dependency. Every card, the status timeline, the audit trail and the field-diff table are static markup; the composer's "Add" control has no <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> wrapper or script wiring either way, so it is illustrative only, never a working control, regardless of JS</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 1 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/kv'}>Key-value facts</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/dashboard'}>Cards</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/approval-workflow'}>Timeline & audit</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/byline'}>Byline</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Related links={[["/components/ordered-list", "Ordered list"], ["/components/byline", "Byline"], ["/components/approval-workflow", "Timeline & audit"], ["/patterns/approval", "Approval workflow"], ["/patterns/list-report", "List report"], ["/patterns/detail-form", "Multi-column detail form (the edit counterpart)"], ["/patterns/output-form", "Issued document (printing or emailing this record)"]]} />
</Gallery>
